spec/US-01.md:71:| Q-US01-05 | Require unique stable field identifiers independent of label and order. On config changes, discard removed-field values and values for changed identifiers, preserve values for reordered fields and updated labels/help, initialize new fields empty or with configured defaults, preserve compatible values and revalidate after validation changes, preserve type-changed values only when compatible, and clear removed select options. Revalidate the whole form, remove removed/incompatible values from active persistence and summary, and block progress while invalid. | AC-US01-06, AC-US01-09, AC-US01-12, AC-US01-14, T-US01-07, T-US01-09, T-US01-12, T-US01-14 |
spec/US-01.md:72:| Q-US01-06 | Keep an in-memory configuration cache during the quote session and refresh it on app reload and country switch. | AC-US01-05, AC-US01-09, T-US01-06, T-US01-09 |
spec/US-01.md:134:Reconcile values by stable field identifier. Discard values for removed fields and for identifiers that changed. Preserve values when fields are reordered or labels/help text change. Initialize new fields empty or from a configured default. Preserve compatible values after validation-rule changes and revalidate them. After a field type change, preserve a value only if it is compatible with the new type, otherwise clear it. Clear a select value when its option is removed. Remove discarded or incompatible values from active persisted state and from any quote summary. Prevent progression whenever the reconciled form is invalid.
